From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller: a radio follows the box, not the address
Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>

Re-parent a known radio when it reports under a different node.

These boards have no stable hardware MAC, so a node draws a fresh AL-MAC on
every boot: a box that comes back is a stranger. The controller files a new
node object for the new address - and the radios stay on the old one, because
cntlr_node_add_radio() finds them by ruid and hands them back untouched:

	r = cntlr_find_radio(c, macaddr);
	if (r) {
		r->invalidate = 0;
		return r;		/* r->agent still points at the old node */
	}

The new node therefore never receives a radio, and the old one is kept alive by
the reports of the box that left it: patch 961 marks a node's radios
invalidate=1 before parsing a live Topology Response and sweeps what the agent
did not confirm, and the line above clears that mark. The confirmation arrives
under the NEW address while the radios hang off the OLD object, so the sweep on
the old node never fires. The ghost is refreshed by its successor.

Measured 2026-08-20, three-node lab, after one agent was power-cycled:

  model (map.controller status)   aa:f5=3  92:fd=3  2e:c5=3  de:36=0
  database (mapc.db)              aa:f5=3  92:fd=3  2e:c5=3  de:36=0

de:36 is the returning box and holds nothing; 92:fd is the address it used
before the reboot and holds all three of its radios - and was the FRESHER of
the two, last_seen 15 s against 54 s. No age test can separate them, which is
why this ghost showed a green dot where every ghost before it had been orange.
The topology view drew the returning node's child hanging off the dead half.

This is not the duplicate-node class that patches 963 and 964 close. Those are
two objects sharing ONE AL-MAC, where mac_table points at exactly one and the
other can never be filled in. Here both addresses are legitimate and both are in
mac_table; what is stale is the association between a box and the name it used
last time.

The radio is the stable half. A ruid comes from the hardware and survives the
reboot - verified across the same power cycle - so a radio reporting under a
different node is not an error to reject but a box that has been renamed. Move
it, with everything that points back at the node: the list membership, r->agent,
and the agent pointer in every fBSS/bBSS beneath it. Miss the last one and the
ghost simply moves down a level.

Nothing else needs changing. The orphan stops receiving its radios' reports,
expires after NODE_EXPIRE_TIME (cntlr.h: 180 s) and cntlr_clean_node() reaps it
- correctly, since it owns its own mac_table entry. The persistence layer needs
no patch either: sync_radio_row() already carries
ON CONFLICT(ruid) DO UPDATE SET agent_almac=excluded.agent_almac, so the
database follows the model on the next sync.

--- a/src/cntlr.c
+++ b/src/cntlr.c
@@ -948,6 +948,32 @@ static struct wifi_radio_element *cntlr_alloc_wifi_radio(
 	return radio_el;
 }
 
+/* Hand a radio, and everything hanging off it, to another node object.
+ *
+ * Called when a box comes back under a new AL-MAC. Three things point at the
+ * node and all three have to move together; the BSS list is the one that is
+ * easy to forget, and forgetting it only moves the ghost one level down.
+ */
+static void cntlr_radio_reparent(struct netif_radio *r, struct node *n)
+{
+	struct netif_iface *iface = NULL;
+
+	if (!r || !n || r->agent == n)
+		return;
+
+	info("%s: radio " MACFMT " moves from " MACFMT " to " MACFMT
+	     " (same box, new AL-MAC)\n", __func__,
+	     MAC2STR(r->radio_el->macaddr),
+	     MAC2STR(r->agent->almacaddr), MAC2STR(n->almacaddr));
+
+	list_del(&r->list);
+	list_add(&r->list, &n->radiolist);
+	r->agent = n;
+
+	list_for_each_entry(iface, &r->iflist, list)
+		iface->agent = n;
+}
+
 struct netif_radio *cntlr_node_add_radio(struct controller *c, struct node *n,
 		uint8_t *macaddr)
 {
@@ -965,7 +991,9 @@ struct netif_radio *cntlr_node_add_radio(struct controller *c, struct node *n,
 	r = cntlr_find_radio(c, macaddr);
 	if (r) {
 		r->invalidate = 0;
+		if (r->agent != n)
+			cntlr_radio_reparent(r, n);
 		return r;
 	}
 
 	r = calloc(1, sizeof(*r));
